 fast and I just have to be ready for  it I see guys is somebody with a world  of potential and the sky is really the  limit but also you know there's a short  time to get there and has to be  deliberate and making those goals  achievable the training here in the  States is different because they really  like focused and my training really  dedicated themselves to help me get  better as a player one thing that we  wanted to really work on getting him to  be more NBA ready which means you know  can he handle the NBA pace of the game  physicality can they use this length in  a meaningful way  does he stretch the floor consistently  can he guard players can he garden the  post can he guard off switches coach  person coach Rob Jeremiah jive been  helping me a lot to helping me prepare  and I just I just get my confidence from  my workouts from my practices I think  for him to come become more physical a  lot of it's gonna take some work at p3  which he's working at every day they do  a great job kind of sports science and  strength and conditioning to develop him  off the court which i think is really  really important here at p3 we assess  our athletes we know what the needs are  so with Ty I think from from this point  on it's just a matter continue to  develop the strength develop that power  he's gonna be playing and matching up  against guys who are bigger than him so  making sure that he is able to match  that intensity on the court but also  making sure that he stays healthy too to  be able to compete year-round that was a  moment in time for him at basketball  Without Borders where all 30 NBA teams  are there there's high-level kids that  are his age that are there and he's able  to see you know I didn't make the first  team I wasn't MVP I wasn't on the first  team all camp and so what are the things  I need to do to improve and so now  you're able to look at positive feedback  from GM Scouts it was good  I do I had the opportunity to play  against the best players all over the  world and to be coached by great coaches  what are the gaps what's gonna help him  get there and I think he took it to  heart you know I think he saw kind of  where he was and was able to size  himself up a little bit and now he's  able to take a step forward because he's  grounded in reality he's not caught kind  of in the hype world you know potential  is something people talk about a lot  right potential potential potential  there's always a point though where you  have to start turning a corner and  potential assets become reality and for  him he's starting to approach that phase  and I think he understands that and so  as long as he continues to move forward  and progress it's got every every  opportunity in the world to be a good  NBA player my ultimate dream is to make  it to the NBA and I also want to  represent the Philippines on  international tournaments I just want to  show that Philippines is part of the  basketball world I appreciate those  people who follow me and my journey  knowing that all my fellow Filipinos  from my country you know supporting me  and following me and I just use it as a  motivation inspiration just to work even  harder to make them proud  [Music]

